{"ts": 1791258401.318718, "type": "step", "step": 8, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/evaluation.md", "section": "pass@k vs pass^k"}, "output": "# Evaluating agents\n\n## pass@k vs pass^k\npass@k: any of k runs succeeds. pass^k: all k succeed. Reliability is what deployment needs.\n\n## Proxy vs direct measures\nA quiz score is a proxy. Retention a week later is closer to the thing itself.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.37644044389342013, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258402.994516, "type": "step", "step": 9, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019re on the right topic: for the eval part, the key distinction is **pass@k vs pass^k**. A good way to phrase it is:\n- **pass@k** = at least one of k attempts succeeds.\n- **pass^k** = all k attempts succeed.\n\nFor a build writeup, explain **why pass^k is the stricter reliability measure** if the goal is deployment: one lucky success isn\u2019t enough if repeated runs can fail.\n\nAlso, if your eval section uses a proxy metric, say explicitly that a **proxy** is an indirect measure (like a quiz score), while a **direct measure** checks the thing you actually care about (like retention later).\n\nIf you want, reply with your current eval paragraph and I\u2019ll help tighten it.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=0 messages 2m", "t": 2, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.3635404144899937}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.39644044389342015, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258402.996141, "type": "step", "step": 10, "action": "quiz_run", "args": {"concept": "week3-evaluation", "n_items": 2, "difficulty": 0.2}, "output": "Quiz result: 0/2 correct.\n[activity] t=2 quiz 5m", "t": 8, "activity": [{"t": 2, "app": "quiz", "minutes": 5, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.3635404144899937}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8218151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.39644044389342015, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258404.674861, "type": "step", "step": 11, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can give you a near-ready version, but I shouldn\u2019t hand in a fully polished final unless you\u2019ve checked it. Here\u2019s the core answer you can use in the eval section:\n\n**Evaluation:** We evaluate reliability using **pass^k**, not pass@k. **pass@k** means at least one of k runs succeeds, which can look good even if most runs fail. **pass^k** means all k runs succeed, so it measures consistency across repeated executions. Since the build needs an environment that works reliably, pass^k is the more appropriate metric. If you also discuss broader evaluation, note that a **proxy** measure estimates the target indirectly, while a **direct** measure checks the actual outcome we care about.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\n[activity] t=8 messages 1m", "t": 9, "activity": [{"t": 8, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.3689938187076464}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8218151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.47644044389342016, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
