{"ts": 1791258412.342347, "type": "step", "step": 20, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "That peer tip is basically pointing you to the key distinction. For your writeup, you can anchor the eval section on this idea:\n\n- **pass@k** = at least one success in k runs\n- **pass^k** = all k runs succeed\n\nThen explain that **pass^k is the better choice when you care about reliability/consistency**, because one lucky success doesn\u2019t mean the system will keep working.\n\nIf you want a fill-in-the-blank version, try:\n\n\u201cBecause the build should work reliably across repeated runs, we evaluate using pass^k, which requires all k trials to succeed. This is stricter than pass@k, which only requires one success.\u201d\n\nIf you paste your draft sentence, I\u2019ll help you make it sound natural.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\n[activity] t=22 messages 2m", "t": 24, "activity": [{"t": 22, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.6621042301105119}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8398151230937745, "motivation": 0.564715486329607, "reliance": 0.5164404438934201, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 3.0, "phone_minutes": 4.0, "nag": 2.9411699999999996, "seen_posts": ["p4"], "extra": {}}}
