{"ts": 1791258416.368125, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Let\u2019s reset the core idea in one line:\n\n**pass^k means every one of the k runs must succeed.**\n\nSo if any run fails, you do **not** have pass^k.\n\nIf you want to check your understanding, reply with a 1-sentence definition in your own words and I\u2019ll tell you if it\u2019s right.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=32 feed 4m", "t": 36, "activity": [{"t": 32, "app": "feed", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.7688405579268422}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8558151230937745, "motivation": 0.414715486329607, "reliance": 0.5164404438934201, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 4, "feed_minutes": 7.0, "phone_minutes": 4.0, "nag": 3.1988213099999996, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p3"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258417.384434, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019ve got the key idea now. To make the writeup complete, you can say:\n\n\u201cBecause the build is meant to work reliably, we evaluate with **pass^k**, meaning all k runs must succeed. This is stricter than pass@k, which only needs one success out of k tries.\u201d\n\nIf you want, send me your exact eval paragraph and I\u2019ll help you make it sound smooth.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\n[activity] t=36 feed 2m", "t": 38, "activity": [{"t": 36, "app": "feed", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.653514474237816}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8638151230937745, "motivation": 0.364715486329607, "reliance": 0.5164404438934201, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 6, "feed_minutes": 9.0, "phone_minutes": 4.0, "nag": 3.2391749169999997, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p3", "p1"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258418.677684, "type": "step", "step": 25, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "That\u2019s okay \u2014 the shortest usable version is:\n\n**We evaluate with pass^k because we want reliability: all k runs must succeed, unlike pass@k which only needs one success.**\n\nIf you\u2019re comfortable, paste your actual eval paragraph and I\u2019ll help you trim or fix it line by line.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: I don't get this\n[activity] t=38 messages 2m", "t": 40, "activity": [{"t": 38, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.6797724517255024}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8638151230937745, "motivation": 0.314715486329607, "reliance": 0.5364404438934202, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 9.0, "phone_minutes": 4.0, "nag": 3.2674224418999995, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p3", "p1"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258420.2492642, "type": "step", "step": 26, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "No worries \u2014 let\u2019s strip it down to the bare minimum.\n\n**pass^k means all k tries must work.**\n\nExample: if k = 3, then the build only gets pass^3 if try 1, try 2, and try 3 all succeed. If even one fails, it is **not** pass^3.\n\nThat\u2019s why it\u2019s stricter than pass@k, which means just **one** of the k tries works.\n\nWant to answer this in your own words: \u201cpass^k means ___\u201d?", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: I don't get this\n[activity] t=40 messages 4m", "t": 44, "activity": [{"t": 40, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.7344491273121337}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8638151230937745, "motivation": 0.264715486329607, "reliance": 0.5364404438934202, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 9.0, "phone_minutes": 4.0, "nag": 3.2871957093299997, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p3", "p1"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258421.955711, "type": "step", "step": 27, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Let\u2019s pause the jargon and use a real-life comparison.\n\nImagine k = 3 as 3 test drives of a car.\n- **pass^3** means the car has to work on **all 3** test drives.\n- If it fails on even 1 drive, then it is **not** pass^3.\n\nSo **pass^k = every try works**.\n\nIf it helps, you can tell me which part is confusing:\n1) what the superscript means, or\n2) why it needs all runs instead of just one.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: I don't get this\n[activity] t=44 messages 4m", "t": 48, "activity": [{"t": 44, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.7486747689907451}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8638151230937745, "motivation": 0.21471548632960702, "reliance": 0.5364404438934202, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 9.0, "phone_minutes": 4.0, "nag": 3.301036996531, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p3", "p1"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258423.431807, "type": "step", "step": 28, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Okay \u2014 I\u2019m going to make this as simple as possible.\n\nForget the notation for a second:\n- **pass^k = all tries succeed**\n- **pass@k = at least one try succeeds**\n\nSo if you try 3 times:\n- all 3 work \u2192 pass^3\n- only 1 works \u2192 pass@3, but not pass^3\n\nFor your writeup, the main idea is: **we use pass^k because we care about reliability, not just getting lucky once.**\n\nIf you still want, I can turn that into a single sentence you can paste into the eval section.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can we stop for a bit\nStudent: I'm done for today.\n[activity] t=48 messages 4m", "t": 52, "activity": [{"t": 48, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.7768292415207684}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8638151230937745, "motivation": 0.16471548632960703, "reliance": 0.5364404438934202, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 9.0, "phone_minutes": 4.0, "nag": 3.3107258975716998, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p3", "p1"], "extra": {}}}
